IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `salsl-dates`
IMPORT `salsl-core`
IMPORT `salsl-seat`

-- Long Service Leave Act 1987 (SA) -- cases for the seat of the worker (salsl-seat.l4). Every expected value was worked
-- by hand from the deposited text (the section is named on each group), never copied from the encoding's output; day
-- counts are shown where they matter. Edges: 10 years and 9 (and 9.99); 7 years and 6 (and 6.9); the anniversary day
-- and the day before, from 1 March and from 29 February; 2 months from 31 December and 15 June, and the day after
-- (s 6(1)(i)); 12 months from 29 February (s 6(3)); 60 days before 1 March in a common and a leap year (s 7(3)); the
-- day before leave and the first day of leave (s 10(6)); the last day of leave and the day after (s 14(1)); the day of
-- termination and the day after (s 8(4)(b)); 14 days, 13 days, review on the 14th and 15th day (s 12); 3 years from
-- 15 March and 29 February, and the day after (ss 10(2)(c), 13(4), 15(2)); s 5(6) using up the entitlement exactly.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases: the worker`

-- Any date, for an input the question does not read.
`ANY` MEANS `the date` 1 1 2000

§§ `ss 3, 9, 16 -- does the Act cover me`

#ASSERT `Does the Act cover me` TRUE `none` FALSE EQUALS `yes: you are a worker and the Act applies to you (ss 3(1), 16)`
#ASSERT `Does the Act cover me` FALSE `none` FALSE EQUALS `no: the Act applies to workers, and a worker means a person employed under a contract of service (s 3(1)); a contractor engaged under a contract for services is not one`
#ASSERT `Does the Act cover me` TRUE `an entitlement under another Act` FALSE EQUALS `no: the Act does not apply to a worker with a long service leave entitlement under some other Act (s 16(a))`
#ASSERT `Does the Act cover me` TRUE `an entitlement under a fair work instrument under the Fair Work Act 2009 of the Commonwealth` FALSE EQUALS `no: the Act does not apply to a worker with a long service leave entitlement under a fair work instrument under the Fair Work Act 2009 of the Commonwealth, such as a modern award or enterprise agreement that provides it (s 16(b))`
#ASSERT `Does the Act cover me` TRUE `an entitlement under an instrument given continuing effect under the Fair Work transitional Act 2009 of the Commonwealth` TRUE EQUALS `no: the Act does not apply to a worker with a long service leave entitlement under an instrument given continuing effect under the Fair Work (Transitional Provisions and Consequential Amendments) Act 2009 of the Commonwealth (s 16(c))`
#ASSERT `Does the Act cover me` TRUE `none` TRUE EQUALS `yes, but under a SAET determination your long service leave is worked out by reference to the award, agreement or scheme it names, and that entitlement is enforceable as if it arose under this Act (s 9(3), (5))`
-- Not a worker is answered first, whatever else is said.
#ASSERT `Does the Act cover me` FALSE `an entitlement under a fair work instrument under the Fair Work Act 2009 of the Commonwealth` TRUE EQUALS `no: the Act applies to workers, and a worker means a person employed under a contract of service (s 3(1)); a contractor engaged under a contract for services is not one`

§§ `s 4 -- service in and outside the State`

#ASSERT `Does my service accrue under the Act` `in South Australia` FALSE EQUALS `yes: this service accrues long service leave under the Act, s 4(1) paragraph` "(a)"
#ASSERT `Does my service accrue under the Act` `outside South Australia while predominantly employed in South Australia` FALSE EQUALS `yes: this service accrues long service leave under the Act, s 4(1) paragraph` "(b)"
#ASSERT `Does my service accrue under the Act` `outside South Australia under a contract of employment whose proper law is South Australian law` TRUE EQUALS `yes, this service accrues under s 4(1), but as you also have an entitlement under a corresponding law (of the Commonwealth, another State or Territory, or another country) you may elect to take it under this Act or under that law, not both (s 4(2)); s 4(1) paragraph` "(c)"
#ASSERT `Does my service accrue under the Act` `in South Australia` TRUE EQUALS `yes, this service accrues under s 4(1), but as you also have an entitlement under a corresponding law (of the Commonwealth, another State or Territory, or another country) you may elect to take it under this Act or under that law, not both (s 4(2)); s 4(1) paragraph` "(a)"
#ASSERT `Does my service accrue under the Act` `outside South Australia otherwise` FALSE EQUALS `s 4(1) does not reach this service: it lists service in South Australia, service outside it while predominantly employed in it, and service outside it under a contract governed by South Australian law, and the Act says nothing of other service`
#ASSERT `Does my service accrue under the Act` `outside South Australia otherwise` TRUE EQUALS `s 4(1) does not reach this service: it lists service in South Australia, service outside it while predominantly employed in it, and service outside it under a contract governed by South Australian law, and the Act says nothing of other service`

§§ `s 6(1), (2) -- breaks and absences`

#ASSERT `Did this break keep my service continuous` `a break my employer brought about, after which I was re-employed under an order of a court or SAET` FALSE `ANY` `ANY` EQUALS `continuous, and the time counts as service: s 6(1) paragraph` "(a)"
#ASSERT `Did this break keep my service continuous` `a break my employer brought about, after which I was re-employed under an order of a court or SAET` TRUE `ANY` `ANY` EQUALS `no: SAET has ordered that this break does affect your continuity of service (s 6(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Did this break keep my service continuous` `a break my employer brought about to avoid an obligation under the Act or a long service leave award, agreement or scheme` FALSE `ANY` `ANY` EQUALS `continuous, and the time counts as service: s 6(1) paragraph` "(b)"
#ASSERT `Did this break keep my service continuous` `an absence allowed by my contract of service` FALSE `ANY` `ANY` EQUALS `continuous, and the time counts as service: s 6(1) paragraph` "(c)"
#ASSERT `Did this break keep my service continuous` `an absence through illness or injury` FALSE `ANY` `ANY` EQUALS `continuous, and the time counts as service: s 6(1) paragraph` "(d)"
#ASSERT `Did this break keep my service continuous` `long service leave or annual leave` FALSE `ANY` `ANY` EQUALS `continuous, and the time counts as service: s 6(1) paragraph` "(e)"
#ASSERT `Did this break keep my service continuous` `another kind of leave` FALSE `ANY` `ANY` EQUALS `continuous, but the time away is not counted in your period of service: s 6(1) and (2), paragraph` "(f)"
#ASSERT `Did this break keep my service continuous` `a stand-down by my employer for slackness in trade, after which I was re-employed by that employer` FALSE `ANY` `ANY` EQUALS `continuous, but the time away is not counted in your period of service: s 6(1) and (2), paragraph` "(g)"
#ASSERT `Did this break keep my service continuous` `a break arising from an industrial dispute, after which I returned under the settlement or was re-employed when it was settled` FALSE `ANY` `ANY` EQUALS `continuous, but the time away is not counted in your period of service: s 6(1) and (2), paragraph` "(h)"
-- s 6(1)(i): 31 December 2025 plus two months is 28 February 2026 (fork F1: the shorter month's last day).
#ASSERT `Did this break keep my service continuous` `another break my employer brought about, after which I returned or was re-employed by that employer` FALSE (`the date` 31 12 2025) (`the date` 28 2 2026) EQUALS `continuous, but the time away is not counted in your period of service: s 6(1) and (2), paragraph` "(i)"
#ASSERT `Did this break keep my service continuous` `another break my employer brought about, after which I returned or was re-employed by that employer` FALSE (`the date` 31 12 2025) (`the date` 1 3 2026) EQUALS `no: s 6(1)(i) preserves continuity only where you return or are re-employed within two months of the break; the last day was` (`the date` 28 2 2026)
-- 15 June 2026 plus two months is 15 August 2026.
#ASSERT `Did this break keep my service continuous` `another break my employer brought about, after which I returned or was re-employed by that employer` FALSE (`the date` 15 6 2026) (`the date` 15 8 2026) EQUALS `continuous, but the time away is not counted in your period of service: s 6(1) and (2), paragraph` "(i)"
#ASSERT `Did this break keep my service continuous` `another break my employer brought about, after which I returned or was re-employed by that employer` FALSE (`the date` 15 6 2026) (`the date` 16 8 2026) EQUALS `no: s 6(1)(i) preserves continuity only where you return or are re-employed within two months of the break; the last day was` (`the date` 15 8 2026)
#ASSERT `Did this break keep my service continuous` `a break I brought about myself, such as resigning, after which I was re-employed` FALSE (`the date` 15 6 2026) (`the date` 20 6 2026) EQUALS `s 6(1) does not reach a break you brought about yourself, and the Act says nothing more; service must be continuous (s 3(1), service), so check whether another paragraph applies`

§§ `ss 3(3), 6(3), 6(4) -- other periods`

-- s 6(3): 30 June 2025 plus 12 months is 30 June 2026.
#ASSERT `Does this other period count as my service` `an apprenticeship with this employer` (`the date` 30 6 2025) (`the date` 30 6 2026) EQUALS `yes: it counts as service, under` "s 6(3)"
#ASSERT `Does this other period count as my service` `an apprenticeship with this employer` (`the date` 30 6 2025) (`the date` 1 7 2026) EQUALS `no: the contract with the employer was entered into more than 12 months after the apprenticeship was completed (s 6(3)); the last day was` (`the date` 30 6 2026)
-- 29 February 2024 plus 12 months is 28 February 2025 (fork F1).
#ASSERT `Does this other period count as my service` `an apprenticeship with this employer` (`the date` 29 2 2024) (`the date` 28 2 2025) EQUALS `yes: it counts as service, under` "s 6(3)"
#ASSERT `Does this other period count as my service` `an apprenticeship with this employer` (`the date` 29 2 2024) (`the date` 1 3 2025) EQUALS `no: the contract with the employer was entered into more than 12 months after the apprenticeship was completed (s 6(3)); the last day was` (`the date` 28 2 2025)
#ASSERT `Does this other period count as my service` `service in the Armed Forces of the Commonwealth, other than the Permanent Forces` `ANY` `ANY` EQUALS `yes: it counts as service, under` "s 6(4), as service with the employer by whom you were last employed"
#ASSERT `Does this other period count as my service` `service in the Permanent Forces` `ANY` `ANY` EQUALS `no: service in the Permanent Forces is excepted (s 6(4))`
#ASSERT `Does this other period count as my service` `service with an employer that took over or acquired the business, or part of it, of the other` `ANY` `ANY` EQUALS `yes: it counts as service, under` "s 3(1) (service) and s 3(3)(a), as long as it is continuous"
#ASSERT `Does this other period count as my service` `service with a related corporation` `ANY` `ANY` EQUALS `yes: it counts as service, under` "s 3(1) (service) and s 3(3)(b), as long as it is continuous"
#ASSERT `Does this other period count as my service` `service with a chain of such employers` `ANY` `ANY` EQUALS `yes: it counts as service, under` "s 3(1) (service) and s 3(3)(c), as long as it is continuous"
#ASSERT `Does this other period count as my service` `service with an unrelated employer` `ANY` `ANY` EQUALS `no: service means continuous service with the same employer or with related employers (s 3(1)), and this employer is neither`

§§ `s 5(7) -- completed years`

-- 1 March 2015 to 28 February 2025, both days counted: the day after is 1 March 2025, the 10th anniversary.
#ASSERT `How many completed years of service do I have` (`the date` 1 3 2015) (`the date` 28 2 2025) 0 0 EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `How many completed years of service do I have` (`the date` 1 3 2015) (`the date` 27 2 2025) 0 0 EQUALS 9
-- One day not counted moves the first day to 2 March 2015: 9 years.
#ASSERT `How many completed years of service do I have` (`the date` 1 3 2015) (`the date` 28 2 2025) 1 0 EQUALS 9
-- One day added moves the first day to 28 February 2015: to 27 February 2025 is 10 years.
#ASSERT `How many completed years of service do I have` (`the date` 1 3 2015) (`the date` 27 2 2025) 0 1 EQUALS 10
-- From 29 February 2016: the anniversary in 2026 is 1 March, so a year completes at the end of 28 February.
#ASSERT `How many completed years of service do I have` (`the date` 29 2 2016) (`the date` 28 2 2026) 0 0 EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `How many completed years of service do I have` (`the date` 29 2 2016) (`the date` 27 2 2026) 0 0 EQUALS 9
#ASSERT `How many completed years of service do I have` (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 31 12 2019) 0 0 EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `How many completed years of service do I have` (`the date` 1 1 2020) (`the date` 31 12 2019) 0 0 EQUALS 0

§§ `s 5(1), (6) -- the entitlement`

#ASSERT `Am I entitled to long service leave` 10 0 EQUALS `entitled (s 5(1)): the weeks accrued, and the weeks remaining after leave taken and payments in lieu (s 5(6)), are` 13 13
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to long service leave` 9 0 EQUALS `no: the entitlement to long service leave arises at 10 years of service (s 5(1)), and your completed years are` 9
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to long service leave` 9.99 0 EQUALS `no: the entitlement to long service leave arises at 10 years of service (s 5(1)), and your completed years are` 9
-- 15 years: 13 + 1.3 x 5 = 19.5 weeks.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to long service leave` 15 0 EQUALS `entitled (s 5(1)): the weeks accrued, and the weeks remaining after leave taken and payments in lieu (s 5(6)), are` 19.5 19.5
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to long service leave` 15 13 EQUALS `entitled (s 5(1)): the weeks accrued, and the weeks remaining after leave taken and payments in lieu (s 5(6)), are` 19.5 6.5
-- 12.7 years is 12 completed: 13 + 2.6 = 15.6 weeks; less 2.6 taken leaves 13.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to long service leave` 12.7 2.6 EQUALS `entitled (s 5(1)): the weeks accrued, and the weeks remaining after leave taken and payments in lieu (s 5(6)), are` 15.6 13
-- More taken (in anticipation) than accrued: nothing remains.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to long service leave` 10 20 EQUALS `entitled (s 5(1)): the weeks accrued, and the weeks remaining after leave taken and payments in lieu (s 5(6)), are` 13 0
-- From dates: 1 March 2015 to 28 February 2025 is 10 years.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to long service leave` (`How many completed years of service do I have` (`the date` 1 3 2015) (`the date` 28 2 2025) 0 0) 0 EQUALS `entitled (s 5(1)): the weeks accrued, and the weeks remaining after leave taken and payments in lieu (s 5(6)), are` 13 13

§§ `s 5(1a) -- cashing out`

`YESCASH` MEANS `yes: you are entitled to the payment in lieu (s 5(1a)); it is worked out at your ordinary weekly rate of pay immediately before it is made, without accommodation (s 8(3a)(a)); a change in your rate within the period of the leave cashed out brings a further payment (s 8(3a)(b)); your employer must give you a copy of the signed record (s 10(2a)(b)) and a statement in Form 3 of the Regulations of the leave cashed out and the days remaining (s 10(7), reg 4(4))`

#ASSERT `Can I cash out my long service leave` 10 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `YESCASH`
#ASSERT `Can I cash out my long service leave` 9 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: only a worker entitled to long service leave under s 5(1), from 10 years of service, can cash it out (s 5(1a)); your completed years are` 9
#ASSERT `Can I cash out my long service leave` 9.5 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: only a worker entitled to long service leave under s 5(1), from 10 years of service, can cash it out (s 5(1a)); your completed years are` 9
#ASSERT `Can I cash out my long service leave` 12 FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: the agreement must be an individual agreement, negotiated between you and your employer (s 5(1a); s 3(1), individual agreement)`
#ASSERT `Can I cash out my long service leave` 12 TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: the agreement must be recorded in writing and signed by both you and your employer (s 5(1a))`
#ASSERT `Can I cash out my long service leave` 12 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: the agreement must be made after the entitlement to the leave cashed out has accrued to you (s 5(1a))`

§§ `s 3(2), (4) -- the ordinary weekly rate of pay`

#ASSERT `What is my ordinary weekly rate of pay` `a weekly rate` 1000 0 0 0 0 FALSE 0 `long service leave` EQUALS `your ordinary weekly rate of pay, in dollars a week, and the provision, are` 1000 "s 3(2)"
#ASSERT `What is my ordinary weekly rate of pay` `a weekly rate` 1000 0 0 0 0 TRUE 150 `long service leave` EQUALS `your ordinary weekly rate of pay, in dollars a week, and the provision, are` 1150 "s 3(2), with the weekly value of accommodation added under s 3(2)(c)"
#ASSERT `What is my ordinary weekly rate of pay` `a weekly rate` 1000 0 0 0 0 TRUE 150 `a payment in lieu on termination` EQUALS `your ordinary weekly rate of pay, in dollars a week, and the provision, are` 1150 "s 3(2), with the weekly value of accommodation added under s 3(2)(c)"
-- s 8(3a)(a): a payment in lieu by agreement leaves the accommodation out.
#ASSERT `What is my ordinary weekly rate of pay` `a weekly rate` 1000 0 0 0 0 TRUE 150 `a payment in lieu by agreement` EQUALS `your ordinary weekly rate of pay, in dollars a week, and the provision, are` 1000 "s 3(2), without the value of accommodation (s 8(3a)(a))"
-- s 3(2)(a): $62,400 over 52 weeks is $1,200 a week.
#ASSERT `What is my ordinary weekly rate of pay` `commission or another system of payment by result` 0 62400 0 52 0 FALSE 0 `long service leave` EQUALS `your ordinary weekly rate of pay, in dollars a week, and the provision, are` 1200 "s 3(2)(a), (4)"
-- s 3(2)(b): 4,680 hours over 156 weeks is 30 hours a week; at $35 an hour, $1,050.
#ASSERT `What is my ordinary weekly rate of pay` `hourly, varied ordinary hours, casual or part-time at some time in the last three years` 0 0 4680 156 35 FALSE 0 `long service leave` EQUALS `your ordinary weekly rate of pay, in dollars a week, and the provision, are` 1050 "s 3(2)(b), (4)"
-- 3,120 hours over 156 weeks is 20 hours; at $40, $800; with $100 accommodation, $900.
#ASSERT `What is my ordinary weekly rate of pay` `hourly, varied ordinary hours, casual or part-time at some time in the last three years` 0 0 3120 156 40 TRUE 100 `long service leave` EQUALS `your ordinary weekly rate of pay, in dollars a week, and the provision, are` 900 "s 3(2)(b), (4), with the weekly value of accommodation added under s 3(2)(c)"
#ASSERT `What is my ordinary weekly rate of pay` `hourly, varied ordinary hours, casual or part-time at some time in the last three years` 0 0 0 0 40 FALSE 0 `long service leave` EQUALS `it cannot be worked out: averaging under s 3(2)(a) or (b) needs at least one week counted (s 3(4))`
#ASSERT `What is my ordinary weekly rate of pay` `commission or another system of payment by result` 0 1000 0 0 0 FALSE 0 `long service leave` EQUALS `it cannot be worked out: averaging under s 3(2)(a) or (b) needs at least one week counted (s 3(4))`

§§ `s 8(1), (2) -- paying the leave`

#ASSERT `How much should I be paid for my leave` 13 1000 EQUALS 13000
#ASSERT `How much should I be paid for my leave` 1.3 1150 EQUALS 1495
#ASSERT `How much should I be paid for my leave` 0 1150 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Is the way I am paid for my leave allowed` `in advance for the whole period of leave` FALSE EQUALS `yes: a way s 8(2) allows, paragraph` "(a)"
#ASSERT `Is the way I am paid for my leave allowed` `on my usual paydays` FALSE EQUALS `yes: a way s 8(2) allows, paragraph` "(b)"
#ASSERT `Is the way I am paid for my leave allowed` `on my usual paydays` TRUE EQUALS `yes: a way s 8(2) allows, paragraph (b); as you asked in writing, it must be paid by cheque posted to the address you gave (s 8(2)(b))`
#ASSERT `Is the way I am paid for my leave allowed` `another way my employer and I agreed` FALSE EQUALS `yes: a way s 8(2) allows, paragraph` "(c)"
#ASSERT `Is the way I am paid for my leave allowed` `another way I did not agree to` FALSE EQUALS `no: payment must be made in advance, on the usual paydays, or in another way you and your employer agreed (s 8(2))`

§§ `s 8(3), (3a)(b) -- a change in the rate`

-- $50 more a week for 6 weeks: $300.
#ASSERT `What more am I owed after a change in my rate` `leave paid in advance` 1000 1050 6 FALSE EQUALS `your employer must make the adjustment on your return to work (s 8(3)); the difference, in dollars, is` 300
#ASSERT `What more am I owed after a change in my rate` `leave paid on the usual paydays` 1000 1050 6 FALSE EQUALS `the variation must be reflected in your leave pay (s 8(3)); the difference, in dollars, is` 300
-- A fall of $20 a week for 4 weeks is reflected too: -$80.
#ASSERT `What more am I owed after a change in my rate` `leave paid on the usual paydays` 1000 980 4 FALSE EQUALS `the variation must be reflected in your leave pay (s 8(3)); the difference, in dollars, is` (0 MINUS 80)
-- $40 more a week for 13 weeks: $520.
#ASSERT `What more am I owed after a change in my rate` `a payment in lieu by agreement` 1000 1040 13 TRUE EQUALS `your employer must make a further payment that reflects the variation (s 8(3a)(b)), in dollars` 520
#ASSERT `What more am I owed after a change in my rate` `a payment in lieu by agreement` 1000 1040 13 FALSE EQUALS `no: s 8(3a)(b) reaches a variation only within the period, from the payment, equal to the leave cashed out`
#ASSERT `What more am I owed after a change in my rate` `a payment in lieu by agreement` 1000 990 13 TRUE EQUALS `s 8(3a)(b) requires a further payment to you; it does not say that a fall in your rate is recovered from you`
#ASSERT `What more am I owed after a change in my rate` `leave paid in advance` 1000 1000 6 FALSE EQUALS `no variation: the rate did not change`

§§ `s 7(3), (7) -- notice and the length of the leave`

-- Leave from 1 March 2027: 60 days before is 31 December 2026 (28 days of February, 31 of January, 1 of December).
#ASSERT `Did I get enough notice of my leave` (`the date` 31 12 2026) (`the date` 1 3 2027) FALSE EQUALS `enough: at least 60 days notice (s 7(3)); the latest day for the notice was` (`the date` 31 12 2026)
#ASSERT `Did I get enough notice of my leave` (`the date` 1 1 2027) (`the date` 1 3 2027) FALSE EQUALS `less than the 60 days notice s 7(3) says your employer should give; the latest day for the notice was` (`the date` 31 12 2026)
#ASSERT `Did I get enough notice of my leave` (`the date` 1 1 2027) (`the date` 1 3 2027) TRUE EQUALS `shorter notice is allowed, as you and your employer agreed to it (s 7(4)(c))`
#ASSERT `Did I get enough notice of my leave` (`the date` 1 12 2026) (`the date` 1 3 2027) TRUE EQUALS `enough: at least 60 days notice (s 7(3)); the latest day for the notice was` (`the date` 31 12 2026)
-- Leave from 1 March 2028 (a leap year): 60 days before is 1 January 2028 (29 days of February, 31 of January).
#ASSERT `Did I get enough notice of my leave` (`the date` 1 1 2028) (`the date` 1 3 2028) FALSE EQUALS `enough: at least 60 days notice (s 7(3)); the latest day for the notice was` (`the date` 1 1 2028)
#ASSERT `Did I get enough notice of my leave` (`the date` 2 1 2028) (`the date` 1 3 2028) FALSE EQUALS `less than the 60 days notice s 7(3) says your employer should give; the latest day for the notice was` (`the date` 1 1 2028)
-- 13 weeks (91 days) from 1 December 2026 ends on 1 March 2027 (30 + 31 + 28 + 1 = 90 days after).
#ASSERT `What is the last day of my leave` (`the date` 1 12 2026) 91 EQUALS `the date` 1 3 2027
-- 91 days from 1 January 2028 ends on 31 March 2028 (30 + 29 + 31 = 90 days after).
#ASSERT `What is the last day of my leave` (`the date` 1 1 2028) 91 EQUALS `the date` 31 3 2028
#ASSERT `What is the last day of my leave` (`the date` 1 1 2028) 1 EQUALS `the date` 1 1 2028

§§ `s 10(6) -- the statement before leave`

-- Granted 1 October 2026, leave from 1 December 2026: the last day is 30 November 2026.
#ASSERT `Did I get my leave statement in time` (`the date` 1 10 2026) (`the date` 1 12 2026) TRUE (`the date` 30 11 2026) `ANY` EQUALS `the statement was given in time, before the leave started (s 10(6)); the last day was` (`the date` 30 11 2026)
#ASSERT `Did I get my leave statement in time` (`the date` 1 10 2026) (`the date` 1 12 2026) TRUE (`the date` 1 10 2026) `ANY` EQUALS `the statement was given in time, before the leave started (s 10(6)); the last day was` (`the date` 30 11 2026)
#ASSERT `Did I get my leave statement in time` (`the date` 1 10 2026) (`the date` 1 12 2026) TRUE (`the date` 1 12 2026) `ANY` EQUALS `the statement was not given before the leave started, as s 10(6) requires (maximum penalty $200); the last day was` (`the date` 30 11 2026)
#ASSERT `Did I get my leave statement in time` (`the date` 1 10 2026) (`the date` 1 12 2026) FALSE `ANY` (`the date` 30 11 2026) EQUALS `not yet given, and still in time: your employer must give it, in Form 2 of the Regulations, by` (`the date` 30 11 2026)
#ASSERT `Did I get my leave statement in time` (`the date` 1 10 2026) (`the date` 1 12 2026) FALSE `ANY` (`the date` 1 12 2026) EQUALS `the statement was not given before the leave started, as s 10(6) requires (maximum penalty $200); the last day was` (`the date` 30 11 2026)
-- Leave granted to start the same day: a statement that day is not "before the leave is taken".
#ASSERT `Did I get my leave statement in time` (`the date` 1 12 2026) (`the date` 1 12 2026) TRUE (`the date` 1 12 2026) `ANY` EQUALS `the statement was not given before the leave started, as s 10(6) requires (maximum penalty $200); the last day was` (`the date` 30 11 2026)

§§ `s 14(1) -- other work while on leave`

-- Leave of 91 days from 1 December 2026 ends on 1 March 2027.
#ASSERT `May I work another job while on leave` (`the date` 1 12 2026) 91 FALSE (`the date` 2 12 2026) EQUALS `the Act does not forbid this: s 14(1) forbids only other employment in place of the employment in which the leave accrued`
#ASSERT `May I work another job while on leave` (`the date` 1 12 2026) 91 TRUE (`the date` 1 12 2026) EQUALS `no: you must not, while on long service leave, engage in other employment in place of your employment (s 14(1)); this work began during the leave, which is an offence (maximum penalty $1 000); the leave ends on` (`the date` 1 3 2027)
#ASSERT `May I work another job while on leave` (`the date` 1 12 2026) 91 TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2027) EQUALS `no: you must not, while on long service leave, engage in other employment in place of your employment (s 14(1)); this work began during the leave, which is an offence (maximum penalty $1 000); the leave ends on` (`the date` 1 3 2027)
#ASSERT `May I work another job while on leave` (`the date` 1 12 2026) 91 TRUE (`the date` 2 3 2027) EQUALS `s 14(1) does not reach this work: it begins after your leave ends, on` (`the date` 1 3 2027)
#ASSERT `May I work another job while on leave` (`the date` 1 12 2026) 91 TRUE (`the date` 30 11 2026) EQUALS `s 14(1) does not reach work that began before your leave; it does forbid going on with it during the leave in place of your employment`

§§ `ss 5(2)-(7) -- when service ends`

#ASSERT `What am I owed when my service ends` 10 `I resigned lawfully` 0 EQUALS `a payment in lieu of your long service leave (s 5(2)), in weeks of your ordinary weekly rate of pay immediately before the termination (s 8(4)(a))` 13
-- s 5(4) excludes only s 5(3): from 10 years, misconduct does not take away the s 5(2) payment.
#ASSERT `What am I owed when my service ends` 10 `my employer ended it on the ground of my serious and wilful misconduct` 0 EQUALS `a payment in lieu of your long service leave (s 5(2)), in weeks of your ordinary weekly rate of pay immediately before the termination (s 8(4)(a))` 13
-- 9 years: 1.3 x 9 = 11.7 weeks; 7 years: 9.1 weeks.
#ASSERT `What am I owed when my service ends` 9 `I resigned lawfully` 0 EQUALS `a payment of the monetary equivalent of 1.3 weeks leave for each completed year of service (s 5(3)), in weeks of your ordinary weekly rate of pay immediately before the termination (s 8(4)(a))` 11.7
#ASSERT `What am I owed when my service ends` 7 `my employer ended it, not for misconduct` 0 EQUALS `a payment of the monetary equivalent of 1.3 weeks leave for each completed year of service (s 5(3)), in weeks of your ordinary weekly rate of pay immediately before the termination (s 8(4)(a))` 9.1
#ASSERT `What am I owed when my service ends` 6.9 `my employer ended it, not for misconduct` 0 EQUALS `no: a payment on termination arises only from seven completed years of service (s 5(3), (7)), and the completed years are` 6
#ASSERT `What am I owed when my service ends` 6 `I retired` 0 EQUALS `no: a payment on termination arises only from seven completed years of service (s 5(3), (7)), and the completed years are` 6
#ASSERT `What am I owed when my service ends` 8 `my employer ended it on the ground of my serious and wilful misconduct` 0 EQUALS `no: there is no payment under s 5(3), as the contract was terminated on the ground of serious and wilful misconduct (s 5(4)(a))`
#ASSERT `What am I owed when my service ends` 8 `I ended my contract unlawfully` 0 EQUALS `no: there is no payment under s 5(3), as you terminated the contract unlawfully (s 5(4)(b))`
-- Death: 8 years is 10.4 weeks under s 5(3); 12 years is 15.6 weeks under s 5(2); both vest in the personal representative.
#ASSERT `What am I owed when my service ends` 8 `the worker died` 0 EQUALS `the entitlement vests in the personal representative of the worker who died (s 5(5)), in weeks of the ordinary weekly rate of pay immediately before the death (s 8(4)(a)), to be paid on request (s 8(4)(b)); weeks and provision` 10.4 "s 5(3)"
#ASSERT `What am I owed when my service ends` 12 `the worker died` 0 EQUALS `the entitlement vests in the personal representative of the worker who died (s 5(5)), in weeks of the ordinary weekly rate of pay immediately before the death (s 8(4)(a)), to be paid on request (s 8(4)(b)); weeks and provision` 15.6 "s 5(2)"
-- s 5(6): 15.6 less 13 taken is 2.6; less 15.6 taken nothing remains.
#ASSERT `What am I owed when my service ends` 12 `I resigned lawfully` 13 EQUALS `a payment in lieu of your long service leave (s 5(2)), in weeks of your ordinary weekly rate of pay immediately before the termination (s 8(4)(a))` 2.6
#ASSERT `What am I owed when my service ends` 12 `I resigned lawfully` 15.6 EQUALS `no: the leave already taken and payments in lieu already made use up the entitlement (s 5(6))`
-- 8 years with 13 weeks taken in anticipation: 10.4 less 13 leaves nothing; the s 7(6) deduction deals with the excess.
#ASSERT `What am I owed when my service ends` 8 `I resigned lawfully` 13 EQUALS `no: the leave already taken and payments in lieu already made use up the entitlement (s 5(6))`
#ASSERT `What am I owed when my service ends` 8 `I retired` 5 EQUALS `a payment of the monetary equivalent of 1.3 weeks leave for each completed year of service (s 5(3)), in weeks of your ordinary weekly rate of pay immediately before the termination (s 8(4)(a))` 5.4

§§ `s 8(4)(b) -- when the payment on termination is due`

#ASSERT `Was my payment on termination on time` (`the date` 30 6 2026) FALSE FALSE `ANY` TRUE (`the date` 30 6 2026) `ANY` EQUALS `paid in time: on the day of the termination, as s 8(4)(b) requires`
#ASSERT `Was my payment on termination on time` (`the date` 30 6 2026) FALSE FALSE `ANY` TRUE (`the date` 1 7 2026) `ANY` EQUALS `paid late: s 8(4)(b) requires payment immediately on the termination, which was on` (`the date` 30 6 2026)
#ASSERT `Was my payment on termination on time` (`the date` 30 6 2026) FALSE FALSE `ANY` FALSE `ANY` (`the date` 30 6 2026) EQUALS `due today: s 8(4)(b) requires payment immediately on the termination`
#ASSERT `Was my payment on termination on time` (`the date` 30 6 2026) FALSE FALSE `ANY` FALSE `ANY` (`the date` 1 7 2026) EQUALS `not yet paid, and overdue: s 8(4)(b) required payment immediately on the termination, which was on` (`the date` 30 6 2026)
-- Paid the day before the termination counts as paid on it (the helper takes an earlier day as day 0).
#ASSERT `Was my payment on termination on time` (`the date` 30 6 2026) FALSE FALSE `ANY` TRUE (`the date` 29 6 2026) `ANY` EQUALS `paid in time: on the day of the termination, as s 8(4)(b) requires`
#ASSERT `Was my payment on termination on time` (`the date` 30 6 2026) TRUE FALSE `ANY` FALSE `ANY` (`the date` 1 9 2026) EQUALS `not yet due: after a death the payment is made to the personal representative on request (s 8(4)(b)), and no request has been made`
#ASSERT `Was my payment on termination on time` (`the date` 30 6 2026) TRUE TRUE (`the date` 10 8 2026) TRUE (`the date` 10 8 2026) `ANY` EQUALS `paid in time: on the day the personal representative asked, as s 8(4)(b) requires`
#ASSERT `Was my payment on termination on time` (`the date` 30 6 2026) TRUE TRUE (`the date` 10 8 2026) TRUE (`the date` 11 8 2026) `ANY` EQUALS `paid late: s 8(4)(b) requires payment to the personal representative on request, which was made on` (`the date` 10 8 2026)
#ASSERT `Was my payment on termination on time` (`the date` 30 6 2026) TRUE TRUE (`the date` 10 8 2026) FALSE `ANY` (`the date` 10 8 2026) EQUALS `due today: s 8(4)(b) requires payment to the personal representative on request`
#ASSERT `Was my payment on termination on time` (`the date` 30 6 2026) TRUE TRUE (`the date` 10 8 2026) FALSE `ANY` (`the date` 12 8 2026) EQUALS `not yet paid, and overdue: s 8(4)(b) required payment to the personal representative on request, which was made on` (`the date` 10 8 2026)

§§ `s 7(6) -- deduction for leave taken in advance`

#ASSERT `How much can my employer deduct for leave taken in advance` FALSE TRUE 13000 0 EQUALS `no: s 7(6) applies only where you took the leave in anticipation of the entitlement accruing`
#ASSERT `How much can my employer deduct for leave taken in advance` TRUE FALSE 13000 0 EQUALS `no: s 7(6) applies only where the service ended before the entitlement to the leave accrued`
-- 8 years at $1,000: paid $13,000 for 13 weeks; the s 5(3) payment would have been $10,400; difference $2,600.
#ASSERT `How much can my employer deduct for leave taken in advance` TRUE TRUE 13000 10400 EQUALS `your employer may deduct up to this amount, in dollars, from the remuneration payable to you on termination (s 7(6))` 2600
#ASSERT `How much can my employer deduct for leave taken in advance` TRUE TRUE 13000 0 EQUALS `your employer may deduct up to this amount, in dollars, from the remuneration payable to you on termination (s 7(6))` 13000
#ASSERT `How much can my employer deduct for leave taken in advance` TRUE TRUE 10400 10400 EQUALS `nothing may be deducted: what you were paid for the leave is no more than the payment in lieu you would have had (s 7(6))`
#ASSERT `How much can my employer deduct for leave taken in advance` TRUE TRUE 5000 10400 EQUALS `nothing may be deducted: what you were paid for the leave is no more than the payment in lieu you would have had (s 7(6))`

§§ `s 10(2)(c), (5) -- the records`

#ASSERT `Can I see my long service leave records` FALSE `ANY` `ANY` EQUALS `yes: you may inspect the records about you during normal office hours (s 10(5)); your employer must keep them throughout your service and for at least three years after it ends (s 10(2)(c))`
#ASSERT `Can I see my long service leave records` TRUE (`the date` 30 6 2026) (`the date` 30 6 2029) EQUALS `your former employer must keep the records about you until at least this day (s 10(2)(c)); s 10(5) gives the right to inspect to a worker against his or her employer, and does not say whether a former worker has it` (`the date` 30 6 2029)
#ASSERT `Can I see my long service leave records` TRUE (`the date` 30 6 2026) (`the date` 1 7 2029) EQUALS `the three years after your service ended have passed (s 10(2)(c)), so the Act no longer requires the records to be kept; the last day was` (`the date` 30 6 2029)
-- 29 February 2024 plus 3 years is 28 February 2027.
#ASSERT `Can I see my long service leave records` TRUE (`the date` 29 2 2024) (`the date` 28 2 2027) EQUALS `your former employer must keep the records about you until at least this day (s 10(2)(c)); s 10(5) gives the right to inspect to a worker against his or her employer, and does not say whether a former worker has it` (`the date` 28 2 2027)
#ASSERT `Can I see my long service leave records` TRUE (`the date` 29 2 2024) (`the date` 1 3 2027) EQUALS `the three years after your service ended have passed (s 10(2)(c)), so the Act no longer requires the records to be kept; the last day was` (`the date` 28 2 2027)

§§ `s 13 -- an order from SAET`

#ASSERT `Can I apply to SAET for my leave or payment` `the worker himself or herself` FALSE TRUE FALSE `ANY` FALSE `ANY` `ANY` EQUALS `yes: you may apply; the service has not ended, so the three-year limit of s 13(4) has not begun; the s 13(2) paragraph is` "(a)"
#ASSERT `Can I apply to SAET for my leave or payment` `the worker himself or herself` FALSE FALSE FALSE `ANY` FALSE `ANY` `ANY` EQUALS `s 13(1) does not reach this: it applies where leave was not granted in accordance with the Act or a payment due under it was not received`
#ASSERT `Can I apply to SAET for my leave or payment` `someone else` FALSE TRUE FALSE `ANY` FALSE `ANY` `ANY` EQUALS `s 13(2) does not name you as someone who may apply`
#ASSERT `Can I apply to SAET for my leave or payment` `a registered association the worker belongs to, without the worker's consent` FALSE TRUE FALSE `ANY` FALSE `ANY` `ANY` EQUALS `no: a registered association may apply only with the worker's consent (s 13(2)(c))`
#ASSERT `Can I apply to SAET for my leave or payment` `the personal representative of the worker who died` FALSE TRUE FALSE `ANY` FALSE `ANY` `ANY` EQUALS `no: a personal representative may apply only if the worker has died (s 13(2)(b))`
-- Ended 15 March 2024: the last day is 15 March 2027.
#ASSERT `Can I apply to SAET for my leave or payment` `the personal representative of the worker who died` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 15 3 2024) TRUE (`the date` 15 3 2027) `ANY` EQUALS `yes: you may apply, and the application is within three years of the termination (s 13(4)); the s 13(2) paragraph, and the last day` "(b)" (`the date` 15 3 2027)
#ASSERT `Can I apply to SAET for my leave or payment` `the worker himself or herself` FALSE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 15 3 2024) TRUE (`the date` 16 3 2027) `ANY` EQUALS `no: an order cannot be made, as the service was terminated more than three years before the application (s 13(4)); the last day was` (`the date` 15 3 2027)
#ASSERT `Can I apply to SAET for my leave or payment` `the worker himself or herself` FALSE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 15 3 2024) FALSE `ANY` (`the date` 1 1 2027) EQUALS `yes: you may apply, and the application is within three years of the termination (s 13(4)); the s 13(2) paragraph, and the last day` "(a)" (`the date` 15 3 2027)
#ASSERT `Can I apply to SAET for my leave or payment` `the worker himself or herself` FALSE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 15 3 2024) FALSE `ANY` (`the date` 16 3 2027) EQUALS `no: an order cannot be made, as the service was terminated more than three years before the application (s 13(4)); the last day was` (`the date` 15 3 2027)
-- Ended 29 February 2024: the last day is 28 February 2027 (fork F1).
#ASSERT `Can I apply to SAET for my leave or payment` `a registered association the worker belongs to, with the worker's consent` FALSE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 29 2 2024) TRUE (`the date` 28 2 2027) `ANY` EQUALS `yes: you may apply, and the application is within three years of the termination (s 13(4)); the s 13(2) paragraph, and the last day` "(c)" (`the date` 28 2 2027)
#ASSERT `Can I apply to SAET for my leave or payment` `a registered association the worker belongs to, with the worker's consent` FALSE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 29 2 2024) TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2027) `ANY` EQUALS `no: an order cannot be made, as the service was terminated more than three years before the application (s 13(4)); the last day was` (`the date` 28 2 2027)
#ASSERT `Can I apply to SAET for my leave or payment` `the complainant in a prosecution in which the employer was found guilty of not complying with an inspector's notice` FALSE TRUE FALSE `ANY` FALSE `ANY` `ANY` EQUALS `yes: you may apply; the service has not ended, so the three-year limit of s 13(4) has not begun; the s 13(2) paragraph is` "(d)"

#ASSERT `Will SAET accept my account without records` TRUE `the period of my service` FALSE EQUALS `no: s 13(3) applies only if the employer has not kept proper long service leave records as the Act requires`
#ASSERT `Will SAET accept my account without records` FALSE `something else` TRUE EQUALS `s 13(3) does not reach this: it covers only the period of your service and your average weekly hours`
#ASSERT `Will SAET accept my account without records` FALSE `the period of my service` TRUE EQUALS `yes: SAET has ruled that what you say about this will be accepted as proved unless the employer proves otherwise (s 13(3))`
#ASSERT `Will SAET accept my account without records` FALSE `the average hours I worked each week` FALSE EQUALS `possibly: SAET may rule that what you say about this will be accepted as proved unless the employer proves otherwise, if it considers that fairness to you requires it (s 13(3))`

§§ `s 12 -- an inspector's direction`

#ASSERT `By when must my employer comply with the inspector` (`the date` 1 7 2026) 13 FALSE `ANY` FALSE `ANY` `ANY` EQUALS `the notice states fewer than 14 days, which s 12(1) does not allow: the period must be at least 14 days`
-- Received 1 July 2026: review applied for on 15 July (the 14th day) suspends the notice; on 16 July it does not.
#ASSERT `By when must my employer comply with the inspector` (`the date` 1 7 2026) 14 TRUE (`the date` 15 7 2026) FALSE `ANY` (`the date` 16 7 2026) EQUALS `the notice is suspended while SAET reviews it (s 12(4)); if SAET confirms it, your employer must comply within the period SAET specifies, on pain of an offence (s 12(6)(b), maximum penalty $5 000)`
#ASSERT `By when must my employer comply with the inspector` (`the date` 1 7 2026) 14 TRUE (`the date` 16 7 2026) FALSE `ANY` (`the date` 16 7 2026) EQUALS `not complied in time: an offence under s 12(6)(a) (maximum penalty $5 000), unless your employer proves you were not entitled (s 12(7)); the last day was` (`the date` 15 7 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must my employer comply with the inspector` (`the date` 1 7 2026) 14 FALSE `ANY` TRUE (`the date` 15 7 2026) `ANY` EQUALS `your employer complied in time (s 12(1)); the last day was` (`the date` 15 7 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must my employer comply with the inspector` (`the date` 1 7 2026) 14 FALSE `ANY` TRUE (`the date` 16 7 2026) `ANY` EQUALS `your employer complied, but after the period stated in the notice: an offence under s 12(6)(a) (maximum penalty $5 000), unless it proves you were not entitled (s 12(7)); the last day was` (`the date` 15 7 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must my employer comply with the inspector` (`the date` 1 7 2026) 14 FALSE `ANY` FALSE `ANY` (`the date` 10 7 2026) EQUALS `not yet complied, and still in time: your employer must grant the leave or make the payment by` (`the date` 15 7 2026)
-- 30 days from 20 December 2026: 11 days to 31 December, 19 more to 19 January 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must my employer comply with the inspector` (`the date` 20 12 2026) 30 FALSE `ANY` TRUE (`the date` 19 1 2027) `ANY` EQUALS `your employer complied in time (s 12(1)); the last day was` (`the date` 19 1 2027)
#ASSERT `By when must my employer comply with the inspector` (`the date` 20 12 2026) 30 FALSE `ANY` TRUE (`the date` 20 1 2027) `ANY` EQUALS `your employer complied, but after the period stated in the notice: an offence under s 12(6)(a) (maximum penalty $5 000), unless it proves you were not entitled (s 12(7)); the last day was` (`the date` 19 1 2027)

§§ `ss 10-15 -- offences and the time to prosecute`

`OFFENCE` MEANS `a summary offence (s 15(1)); the maximum penalty in dollars, the provision, and the last day to commence a prosecution (s 15(2)), are`

#ASSERT `What is the fine and the time to prosecute` `not keeping the long service leave records` (`the date` 1 7 2026) EQUALS `OFFENCE` 1000 "s 10(1)" (`the date` 1 7 2029)
#ASSERT `What is the fine and the time to prosecute` `not recording a cashing-out agreement in writing, giving me a copy, or keeping it` (`the date` 1 7 2026) EQUALS `OFFENCE` 1000 "s 10(2a)" (`the date` 1 7 2029)
#ASSERT `What is the fine and the time to prosecute` `not passing the records on to a related employer` (`the date` 1 7 2026) EQUALS `OFFENCE` 1000 "s 10(4)" (`the date` 1 7 2029)
#ASSERT `What is the fine and the time to prosecute` `not giving me the statement before my leave` (`the date` 29 2 2024) EQUALS `OFFENCE` 200 "s 10(6)" (`the date` 28 2 2027)
#ASSERT `What is the fine and the time to prosecute` `not giving me the statement when my leave was cashed out` (`the date` 1 7 2026) EQUALS `OFFENCE` 200 "s 10(7)" (`the date` 1 7 2029)
#ASSERT `What is the fine and the time to prosecute` `obstructing an inspector or not complying with an inspector's requirement` (`the date` 1 7 2026) EQUALS `OFFENCE` 5000 "s 11(3)" (`the date` 1 7 2029)
#ASSERT `What is the fine and the time to prosecute` `not complying with an inspector's notice to grant my leave or pay me` (`the date` 1 7 2026) EQUALS `OFFENCE` 5000 "s 12(6)" (`the date` 1 7 2029)
#ASSERT `What is the fine and the time to prosecute` `engaging a worker knowing the worker is on long service leave, so that the worker breaches s 14(1)` (`the date` 1 7 2026) EQUALS `OFFENCE` 1000 "s 14(2)" (`the date` 1 7 2029)
#ASSERT `What is the fine and the time to prosecute` `my own other employment in place of my employment while on long service leave` (`the date` 1 7 2026) EQUALS `OFFENCE` 1000 "s 14(1)" (`the date` 1 7 2029)
